.SH "Macro Definition Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "#define AI_ANIM_H_INC"

.SH "Enumeration Type Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "\fBenum\fP \fBaiAnimBehaviour\fP"
Defines how an animation channel behaves outside the defined time range\&. This corresponds to \fBaiNodeAnim::mPreState\fP and \fBaiNodeAnim::mPostState\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBEnumerator\fP
.in +1c
.TP
\fB\fIaiAnimBehaviour_DEFAULT \fP\fP
The value from the default node transformation is taken 
.TP
\fB\fIaiAnimBehaviour_CONSTANT \fP\fP
The nearest key value is used without interpolation 
.TP
\fB\fIaiAnimBehaviour_LINEAR \fP\fP
The value of the nearest two keys is linearly extrapolated for the current time value\&. 
.TP
\fB\fIaiAnimBehaviour_REPEAT \fP\fP
The animation is repeated\&.
.PP
If the animation key go from n to m and the current time is t, use the value at (t-n) % (|m-n|)\&. 
.TP
\fB\fI_aiAnimBehaviour_Force32Bit \fP\fP
This value is not used, it is just here to force the the compiler to map this enum to a 32 Bit integer 
